{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7128408","formula":"C₂₃H₄₅NO₄","hill":"C23H45NO4","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":23.0,"H":45.0,"N":1.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"(+/-)-palmitoyl carnitine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Palmitoylcarnitine is an ester derivative of carnitine involved in the metabolism of fatty acids. During the tricarboxylic acid cycle (TCA), fatty acids undergo a process known as β-oxidation to produce energy in the form of ATP. β-oxidation occurs primarily within mitochondria, however the mitochondrial membrane prevents the entry of long chain fatty acids (>C10), so the conversion of fatty acids such as palmitic acid is key. Palmitic acid is brought to the cell and once inside the cytoplasm is first converted to Palmitoyl-CoA."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":461,"mass":399.6,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC(=O)OC(CC(=O)[O-])C[N+](C)(C)C","inchikey":"XOMRRQXKHMYMOC-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"3-hexadecanoyloxy-4-(trimethylazaniumyl)butanoate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"461","atoms":73,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":10.111,"y":-0.814,"z":-2.123,"el":"C"},{"x":8.869,"y":-0.831,"z":-3.001,"el":"C"},{"x":7.584,"y":-1.169,"z":-2.241,"el":"C"},{"x":7.179,"y":-0.093,"z":-1.23,"el":"C"},{"x":5.897,"y":-0.432,"z":-0.459,"el":"C"},{"x":4.638,"y":-0.405,"z":-1.33,"el":"C"},{"x":3.359,"y":-0.742,"z":-0.556,"el":"C"},{"x":2.989,"y":0.309,"z":0.495,"el":"C"},{"x":1.599,"y":0.091,"z":1.103,"el":"C"},{"x":1.487,"y":-1.209,"z":1.903,"el":"C"},{"x":0.176,"y":-1.322,"z":2.69,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.059,"y":-1.41,"z":1.791,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.35,"y":-1.701,"z":2.563,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.736,"y":-0.672,"z":3.635,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.851,"y":0.766,"z":3.136,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.898,"y":0.912,"z":2.061,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.031,"y":0.453,"z":2.122,"el